&lt;h3&gt;&lt;em&gt;Multilateralism and a New World Order&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
A conversation with&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://worldleaders.columbia.edu/directory/alexander-stubb" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alexander Stubb&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
President of the Republic of Finland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.law.columbia.edu/faculty/anu-bradford" target="_blank"&gt;Anu Bradford&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Henry L. Moses Professor of Law and International Organization&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
We are living in a time of profound change. The liberal world order that emerged after World War II is unraveling. Global norms are eroding. What comes next will define the rest of the century, so the search is on for a new global framework&amp;mdash;a rebalancing of power.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this conversation, President of the Republic of Finland Alexander Stubb will discuss the shifting center of economic and political power, values-based realism, and how the current moment presents Finland with opportunities to build multilateral cooperation and influence as demonstrated by his global leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;President Stubb is the author of &lt;em&gt;The Triangle of Power: Rebalancing the New World Order&lt;/em&gt;, published by Columbia Global Reports in January 2026.&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
