&lt;p&gt;Join us on &lt;strong&gt;September 25 at 7:00pm (note the earlier time) in Pupin 301 &lt;/strong&gt;for a talk by Prof. Chuck Hailey about the search for dark matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Dark Matter, Antimatter, Black Holes &amp;ndash; Oh My!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abstract: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;ldquo;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dark matter makes up most of the stuff in our Universe, but scientists have no idea what it is made of. In this talk, I will describe the GAPS experiment, which searches for evidence that can lead us to discovering the particle that is dark matter. This talk will take us on a journey, exploring antimatter, dark matter, and primordial black holes as we follow GAPS&amp;rsquo;s deployment from New York to the burning heat of East Texas to the freezing cold of Antarctica, where it was floated high into the atmosphere via balloon to shed light on these mysteries.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;rdquo;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&amp;#39;ll start the evening at &lt;strong&gt;7:00pm &lt;/strong&gt;with some astronomy trivia, followed by the talk and Q&amp;amp;A. From 8:10-9:00pm, we will be outside observing on campus (weather permitting).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
